{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender requests how to add the floor printer; checking account and devices to identify her laptop and floor."
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Welcome to Brightline, Hannah! To add the printer on your floor:\n\n1. Find the printer's name on the label on the front or side of the printer. It looks like BL-PR-FL1 (your floor's number may differ).\n2. On your laptop, open Settings, then Bluetooth & devices, then Printers & scanners, and click Add device.\n3. If the printer shows up in the list, select it. If it doesn't, click \"Add manually\" and type the printer name from the label.\n4. If you print there most often, set it as your default printer.\n5. Print a test page to confirm it works.\n\nYour laptop needs to be in the office or connected to VPN for this to work. If the printer doesn't appear or you can't add it, reply to this ticket with the name on the label and we'll take a look.",
  "internal_note": "Hannah Lee (user 12, Finance, Payroll Specialist, device BL-LT-0112). Ticket is a new-employee how-to request. Followed KB-024 steps and sent them the add-printer instructions. Printer hostname for her floor was not provided in the ticket, so I did not check printer status. If she reports that the printer is listed as offline, follow KB-022. If it is online but cannot be added from her laptop, escalate per KB-024. Account is active and not blocked; must_change_password is set, so she may need a password change if she has not done one yet.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-024"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
